  "content": {
    "title": "Slew of UFC dates official, including likely International Fight Week card",
    "text": "March 25, 2026, 1:13 p.m. ETA slew of UFC event permits were approved by Nevada for dates this summer – including one likely to be International Fight Week.At a monthly meeting Wednesday, the Nevada Athletic Commission approved the following dates for Meta APEX: April 25, May 16, June 6, and June 20. This brings the number of Meta APEX events up to seven in 2026.Additionally, the NAC approved a July 11 event at T-Mobile Arena in Las Vegas. Given the UFC is expected to be in Baku, Azerbaijan on June 27, it's likely the July 11 event will be UFC 329 and mark the return of International Fight Week – and possibly Conor McGregor, who continues to hype the event as a potential landing spot.The current lineups for the newly official Nevada event dates include:April 25: UFC Fight Night 274Aljamain Sterling vs. Youssef ZalalNorma Dumont vs. Joselyne EdwardsTalita Alencar vs. Julia PolastriEric McConico vs. Rodolfo VieiraJafel Filho vs. Lucas RochaRaoni Barcelos vs. Montel JacksonMichelle Montague vs. Mayra Bueno SilvaAllen Frye Jr. vs. Max GimenisDavey Grant vs. Adrian Luna MartinettiSedriques Dumas vs. Jackson McVeyMay 16: UFC Fight Night 276Arnold Allen vs. Melquizael CostaJacqueline Cavalcanti vs. Ketlen VieiraRodolfo Bellato vs. Modestas BukauskasAlice Ardelean vs. Polyana VianaDaniel Barez vs. Luis GuruleCody Brundage vs. Andre PetroskiJune 6: UFC Fight Night 278Gabriel Bonfim vs. Belal MuhammadEdgar Chairez vs. Bruno SilvaBrendan Allen vs. Edmen ShahbazyanJeisla Chaves vs. Yuneisy DubenJune 20: UFC Fight Night 279Kyoji Horiguchi vs. Manel KapeJhonata Diniz vs. Jose LuizJuly 11: UFC 329No fights announced yet.",
